const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"不托管资产，不代表排序公平",en:"Noncustodial settlement does not ensure fair ordering"},body:{zh:"Daian等人把去中心化交易所中的竞争与底层交易排序联系起来。用户保有资产控制权，只说明某些托管依赖被改变，并不保证交易按所有人都认为公平的顺序执行。研究市场设计时，托管、报价、排序和结算需要分别讨论。",en:"Daian and colleagues connect competition on decentralized exchanges to transaction ordering below them. Retaining control of assets changes custody dependencies, not necessarily execution fairness. Custody, quotations, ordering and settlement are separate dimensions of market design."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.05234v1",label:{zh:"2019年arXiv初稿 · §I",en:"2019 arXiv v1 · §I"}}},{title:{zh:"应用层激励可能影响共识层",en:"Application incentives can reach the consensus layer"},body:{zh:"文章关注的不只是某个交易者多支付了多少费用，还包括排序产生的经济激励是否改变区块生产者的行为。交易应用和共识协议不能总被视作互不影响的两层。但具体风险仍依赖当时机制，不能由历史讨论直接推断当前网络状态。",en:"The argument goes beyond fees paid by an individual trader to incentives that ordering opportunities create for block producers. Applications and consensus are not always economically independent. The specific risk still depends on the mechanism studied, not an inference about today's network."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.05234v1",label:{zh:"2019年arXiv初稿 · §I; §II",en:"2019 arXiv v1 · §I; §II"}}},{title:{zh:"Gas用量、单价与总费用分开",en:"Separate gas used, gas price and total fees"},body:{zh:"初稿区分计算消耗的Gas单位、每单位愿付价格及由此形成的费用。Gas上限则约束执行预算，不等于最后实际使用量。比较历史交易成本时，应同时保留数量、价格和计价资产；一个叫Gas的字段不足以重建成本。",en:"The draft separates computational gas units, the price per unit and the resulting fee. A gas limit caps the execution budget rather than reporting actual usage. Historical cost comparisons need quantities, prices and denomination; a single field called gas is insufficient."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.05234v1",label:{zh:"2019年arXiv初稿 · §II.A–B",en:"2019 arXiv v1 · §II.A–B"}}},{title:{zh:"交易所设计包含多个集中化环节",en:"Exchange designs contain distinct coordination points"},body:{zh:"论文讨论的去中心化交易场所仍可能在订单传播、匹配或界面等部分依赖特定运营者，而资金结算交给链上合约。不同设计暴露的机会和观测数据不相同。不能只按DEX标签合并所有场所，再解释为同一种市场结构。",en:"Exchanges in the discussion can rely on particular operators for order dissemination, matching or interfaces while settling through contracts. Designs expose different opportunities and observable data. Pooling venues under a DEX label does not make their market structures equivalent."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.05234v1",label:{zh:"2019年arXiv初稿 · §II.C–E",en:"2019 arXiv v1 · §II.C–E"}}},{title:{zh:"原子执行改变失败模式，不消除成本",en:"Atomic execution changes failure modes, not all costs"},body:{zh:"多笔交换可以放入一次合约交易，使部分步骤失败时整体回退。这与跨场所分开执行、只有一条腿成功的风险不同。编辑解读中仍应把交易资产流入与网络费用分开；原子性不是零成本或无条件净利润的同义词。",en:"Several swaps can execute inside one contract transaction and revert together if a step fails, unlike separately executed legs. Editorial interpretation: keep traded-asset proceeds separate from network fees. Atomicity changes execution failure modes; it does not imply zero cost or unconditional net profit."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.05234v1",label:{zh:"2019年arXiv初稿 · §III.A",en:"2019 arXiv v1 · §III.A"}}},{title:{zh:"可识别子集不是全部MEV",en:"An identifiable subset is not all MEV"},body:{zh:"作者明确聚焦可从单次原子交易辨认的纯收入机会，并把更复杂或不确定的机器人行为留在范围之外。这个取样有助于测量，却不能代表全部排序收益。链上成交记录也不能自动替代未上链订单、被替换请求和传播过程的完整历史。",en:"The measurement focuses on identifiable pure-revenue opportunities within atomic transactions and excludes more complex or nondeterministic bot behavior. This tractable subset is not all ordering value. Editorial caution: settled chain records alone do not reconstruct every pending, replaced or disseminated request."},reference:{url:"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1904.05234v1",label:{zh:"2019年arXiv初稿 · §III.A · p. 4",en:"2019 arXiv v1 · §III.A · p. 4"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读依据2019年初稿，保留后续会议论文引用。历史以太坊的费用与共识环境不代表当前机制；本文用于理解交易排序和测量边界，不提供抢跑操作或收益承诺。",en:"This guide uses the 2019 first draft, separately from the later conference citation. Its historical Ethereum fee and consensus setting is not current-mechanism evidence. The focus is ordering and measurement, not instructions for frontrunning or promised returns."}};export{e as default};
